On Thursday 28 April 2011 10:04:15 A. PIEKARSKI wrote:
> So, my questrion is: Can we use lerfu strings to create fu'ivla?
>
> Examples:
> OF-10: jatnrobufypano
> OF-2: jatnrobufyre

You can't have "y" in a fu'ivla. You could do something like "jatnrxofopano", 
where the "x" is needed for proper type-3 form, the "of" is from the NATO 
code, and the second "o" is there in case the "f" clashes with the first 
consonant of the nacyvla. Another way to name ranks is to mash together 
Chinese and English words to get "jianrale" ("jiang" + "general") for upper 
ranks, and similarly for other ranks, and say "zelmoikle jianrale".

